From 94e9732eabe50e037e5ca9a0e662bbd31ae87016 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: woahwhattheheck <293286387+woahwhattheheck@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 11:47:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] Cast: Fix device discovery and route publication

CastMediaRouteProvider:
- Discover on every valid discovery request that asks for a Cast or
  remote playback category, not only on active scans. MediaRouter clients
  such as the Cast framework request passive discovery, so no devices
  were found until a route chooser forced an active scan.
- Collect receiver application categories from every request without
  duplicates and republish routes when they change, so routes match the
  selector of apps using categoryForCast(appId).
- Make NSD discovery start/stop transitions robust: requests arriving
  while a start or stop is pending are applied from the listener
  callbacks instead of being lost, and a fresh listener is used for each
  discovery run.
- Resolve found services one after the other. NsdManager rejects
  concurrent resolves with FAILURE_ALREADY_ACTIVE, which dropped every
  device but the first when several were on the network.
- Tolerate missing TXT records (only "id" is required) and read device
  capabilities from the "ca" record. Audio-only devices and multizone
  groups are published as speakers.
- Update known devices with the latest resolved record (address, port,
  name, status) instead of keeping the first one.
- Keep all state on the main thread; NSD callbacks previously modified
  the device maps from binder threads while routes were published.
- Publish variable volume and the connection state reported by the route
  controller. Drop the duplicated ACTION_SYNC_STATUS filter.

CastMediaRouteController:
- Connect to the device on the announced service port (multizone groups
  do not listen on 8009), off the main thread.
- Implement select/unselect/release, report connecting/connected/
  disconnected state, read the device volume on select and follow volume
  changes made on the device.
- Implement onSetVolume/onUpdateVolume.
